Package: camview
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: orozcorgint <orozcorgint@users.noreply.github.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Recommends: @RECOMMENDS@
Suggests: @SUGGESTS@
Section: video
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/orozcorgint/camview
Description: lightweight RTSP camera viewer and recorder
 CamView is a native Linux viewer and recorder for RTSP and RTSPS cameras,
 designed for low-power desktops. It displays several cameras in a grid,
 records stream-copy Matroska segments with a global rolling storage limit,
 resumes recordings after a camera reconnect, and supports fullscreen digital
 zoom.
 .
 It uses libmpv for hardware-accelerated decoding and keeps one RTSP session
 per camera for simultaneous viewing and recording. Camera credentials are
 stored locally in ~/.config/camview/config.toml with mode 0600.
